यह उदाहरण जानबूझकर केवल basic directory fields export करता है; अंतिम field list पर product approval चाहिए।

**Integration prerequisite:** नीचे `auditLog` वही existing input लेता है, लेकिन उसका durable write **अलग, bounded audit connection pool** पर होना चाहिए। अन्यथा export transactions shared pool की सारी connections रोककर audit को starvation/deadlock जैसी स्थिति में डाल सकती हैं। Audit record का `count` उसी snapshot की export-eligible rows है—client को वास्तव में मिली rows नहीं। इस semantics को audit contract में दर्ज करें; completion tracking चाहिए तो export ID और अलग outcome event जोड़ें।

SQL cursor के कारण कोई नया streaming package आवश्यक नहीं है।

```ts
import { Router, Response } from 'express';
import type { PoolClient } from 'pg';
import { pool } from '../db';
import { requireRole } from '../auth';
import { auditLog } from '../audit';

const router = Router();

const SORTS = new Map<string, string>([
  ['created_at', 'created_at ASC NULLS LAST, id ASC'],
  ['email', 'email ASC NULLS LAST, id ASC'],
  ['full_name', 'full_name ASC NULLS LAST, id ASC'],
  ['id', 'id ASC'],
]);

const COLUMNS = [
  'id',
  'email',
  'full_name',
  'created_at',
  'last_login_at',
] as const;

type ExportRow = Record<
  (typeof COLUMNS)[number],
  string | number | Date | null
>;

function csvCell(value: ExportRow[keyof ExportRow]): string {
  let text =
    value == null
      ? ''
      : value instanceof Date
        ? value.toISOString()
        : String(value);

  // Conservative spreadsheet protection, including whitespace-prefixed formulas.
  // This intentionally changes dangerous text representations.
  if (/^[\s\uFEFF]*[=+\-@]/u.test(text) || /^[\t\r\n]/u.test(text)) {
    text = "'" + text;
  }

  return `"${text.replace(/"/g, '""')}"`;
}

function csvRow(values: ExportRow[keyof ExportRow][]): string {
  return values.map(csvCell).join(',') + '\r\n';
}

// Honor backpressure; do not leave a drain waiter hanging on disconnect.
function writeChunk(res: Response, chunk: string): Promise<void> {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    function cleanup() {
      res.off('drain', onDrain);
      res.off('close', onClose);
      res.off('error', onError);
    }
    function onDrain() {
      cleanup();
      resolve();
    }
    function onClose() {
      cleanup();
      reject(new Error('Export connection closed'));
    }
    function onError(error: Error) {
      cleanup();
      reject(error);
    }

    res.once('drain', onDrain);
    res.once('close', onClose);
    res.once('error', onError);

    try {
      if (res.destroyed || res.writableEnded) {
        onClose();
      } else if (res.write(chunk)) {
        cleanup();
        resolve();
      }
    } catch (error) {
      onError(error instanceof Error ? error : new Error('Write failed'));
    }
  });
}

router.get('/users/export', requireRole('admin'), async (req, res) => {
  res.setHeader('Cache-Control', 'no-store');
  res.setHeader('X-Content-Type-Options', 'nosniff');

  // Reject even a matching override: this endpoint has no tenant selector.
  if (req.query.tenantId !== undefined) {
    res.status(400).json({ error: 'tenantId override is not supported' });
    return;
  }

  const tenantId = req.user.tenantId;
  if (typeof tenantId !== 'string' || tenantId.length === 0) {
    res.status(403).json({ error: 'Tenant context required' });
    return;
  }

  const sortKey = req.query.sort ?? 'created_at';
  if (typeof sortKey !== 'string' || !SORTS.has(sortKey)) {
    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid sort' });
    return;
  }
  const orderBy = SORTS.get(sortKey)!;

  let client: PoolClient | undefined;
  let inTransaction = false;
  let discardClient = false;
  let disconnected = false;

  const onClose = () => {
    disconnected = true;
  };
  res.once('close', onClose);

  // Bound slow downloads and transaction lifetime.
  // Pool connection acquisition and audit queries also need configured timeouts.
  const deadline = setTimeout(() => {
    disconnected = true;
    res.destroy();
  }, 5 * 60_000);
  deadline.unref();

  function checkConnection() {
    if (disconnected || res.destroyed) {
      throw new Error('Export connection closed');
    }
  }

  try {
    client = await pool.connect();
    checkConnection();

    await client.query(
      'BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL REPEATABLE READ READ ONLY',
    );
    inTransaction = true;

    await client.query("SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '30s'");
    await client.query(
      "SET LOCAL idle_in_transaction_session_timeout = '60s'",
    );

    // Count and cursor use the same snapshot.
    const countResult = await client.query<{ count: string }>(
      'SELECT count(*) AS count FROM users WHERE tenant_id = $1',
      [tenantId],
    );
    const count = Number(countResult.rows[0].count);
    if (!Number.isSafeInteger(count)) {
      throw new Error('Export count out of range');
    }

    // Only the fixed allowlisted fragment is interpolated.
    await client.query(
      `DECLARE users_export_cursor NO SCROLL CURSOR FOR
       SELECT id, email, full_name, created_at, last_login_at
       FROM users
       WHERE tenant_id = $1
       ORDER BY ${orderBy}`,
      [tenantId],
    );

    checkConnection();

    // Must commit durably on the independent audit pool before disclosure.
    await auditLog({
      actor: req.user.id,
      action: 'users.export',
      tenantId,
      count,
    });

    checkConnection();

    res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/csv; charset=utf-8');
    res.setHeader(
      'Content-Disposition',
      'attachment; filename="users.csv"',
    );

    await writeChunk(res, csvRow([...COLUMNS]));

    for (;;) {
      checkConnection();

      // Bounded memory: one batch, not the complete tenant.
      const batch = await client.query<ExportRow>(
        'FETCH FORWARD 1000 FROM users_export_cursor',
      );

      checkConnection();
      if (batch.rows.length === 0) break;

      for (const row of batch.rows) {
        await writeChunk(
          res,
          csvRow(COLUMNS.map((column) => row[column])),
        );
      }
    }

    await client.query('CLOSE users_export_cursor');
    await client.query('COMMIT');
    inTransaction = false;
    res.end();
  } catch (error) {
    // Send diagnostics only to restricted server logs; never log exported rows.
    console.error('users.export failed', {
      actor: req.user.id,
      tenantId,
      error,
    });

    if (!res.destroyed) {
      if (res.headersSent) {
        // A partial CSV must not be followed by JSON or marked successful.
        res.destroy();
      } else {
        res.removeHeader('Content-Disposition');
        res.status(500).type('application/json').json({
          error: 'Unable to export users',
        });
      }
    }
  } finally {
    clearTimeout(deadline);
    res.off('close', onClose);

    if (client) {
      if (inTransaction) {
        try {
          await client.query('ROLLBACK');
        } catch {
          discardClient = true;
        }
      }
      client.release(discardClient);
    }
  }
});

export default router;
```

Production configuration में bounded connection acquisition/audit timeouts, per-tenant export concurrency limits और tenant/sort indexes भी रखें। Streaming memory बचाती है; database sorting cost और लंबे snapshots समाप्त नहीं करती।

## 4. Merge से पहले अनिवार्य tests

1. **Authorization और disclosure integration test:** A का admin B का override नहीं दे सकता; default export में केवल A की rows हों। Injection, unknown sort, array/object query values reject हों। Headers और CSV में credential तथा sensitive HR columns अनुपस्थित हों।

2. **CSV contract test:** Empty tenant header-only CSV दे। Comma, double quote, multiline Hindi नाम, null और dates का independent CSV parser से round-trip जाँचें। Formula और whitespace-prefixed formula inputs neutralized हों; supported spreadsheet applications में formula-execution smoke test करें।

3. **Audit और scale/failure test:** Audit promise pending रहने तक कोई CSV byte न निकले; rejection पर export बंद हो। 1,40,000 synthetic rows और slow consumer के साथ bounded memory/backpressure जाँचें। Mid-stream disconnect तथा DB error पर cursor/transaction/client release हों, response में stack या trailing JSON न आए, और full download में snapshot count के बराबर rows मिलें।
